Once to the tune of a couple of million.

1184
00:47:51,893 --> 00:47:52,234
Devastating.

1185
00:47:52,334 --> 00:47:53,753
Took me a while to survive that one.

1186
00:47:56,094 --> 00:47:57,194
Now, it wasn't all that much,

1187
00:47:57,194 --> 00:47:58,294
but it was all I had.

1188
00:47:59,453 --> 00:48:00,914
I mean, that's when it's much, right?

1189
00:48:00,934 --> 00:48:02,154
When it's all you got.

1190
00:48:02,833 --> 00:48:04,453
If you got three, two go.

1191
00:48:04,594 --> 00:48:05,554
You got one left.

1192
00:48:05,633 --> 00:48:06,753
You ain't looking that bad.

1193
00:48:06,833 --> 00:48:08,253
But when it all goes.

1194
00:48:08,534 --> 00:48:10,494
Has anybody been there when it all went?

1195
00:48:11,114 --> 00:48:11,354
Anybody?

1196
00:48:12,554 --> 00:48:13,854
Come on, the rest of you liars.

1197
00:48:14,193 --> 00:48:14,393
Go ahead.

1198
00:48:16,054 --> 00:48:17,534
Hey, we've all been there, right?

1199
00:48:17,873 --> 00:48:19,174
When it all went.

1200
00:48:21,934 --> 00:48:22,684
Of course, it used to

1201
00:48:22,684 --> 00:48:23,434
be a long time ago, right?

1202
00:48:23,453 --> 00:48:24,583
When you ran out of money,

1203
00:48:24,583 --> 00:48:25,714
